Request Type: GET
Request Host: localhost
--------------------------------------------------------------------
```

As you can see, the middleware ran twice.
Now, if you were to connect to this via another device on your LAN, this problem disappears.

This is also reproducible on Microsoft Edge.
I'm not sure if this is a thing with Windows OS itself or Express, but it's a bit annoying.

### Description

Quoting the only documentation within the code for extending the express types:

```
declare global {
    namespace Express {
        // These open interfaces may be extended in an application-specific manner via declaration merging.
        // See for example method-override.d.ts (https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/blob/master/types/method-override/index.d.ts)
        interface Request {}
        interface Response {}
        interface Locals {}
        interface Application {}
    }
}
