Similar to the issue https://github.com/expressjs/express/issues/3324, but we note that there was something related with the `express.Router()`


The code was like this:

```js
// app.js
const express = require('express');
const routes = require('./routes');
const app = express();

app.get('/healthz', ...); // <-- error after 300+ requests
app.get('/version', ...); // <-- error after 300+ requests
app.use('/', routes);

...

// routes.js
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();

...
```

In order to fix, we changed to:


```js
// app.js
const express = require('express');
const routes = require('./routes');
const app = express();

app.use('/', routes);

...

// routes.js
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();

router.get('/healthz', ...); // <-- fixed, no more errors
router.get('/version', ...); // <-- fixed, no more errors

...
```

